#X text 40 680 u_mother-stub -- impersonates mother.pd on the Mac \, where it does not exist \, and is the dev panel. main-dev.pd instantiates it and main.pd does not \, so the device never sees it., f 58;
#X text 40 775 The one sanctioned exception to C-2: it sends on names mother.pd owns \, which is its purpose., f 58;
#X text 40 860 No cords on the panel: every control binds by its iemgui send name and every readout by its receive \, so graph-on-parent can show the whole face on main-dev.pd (ref/conventions.md \, GUI binding)., f 58;
#X text 640 680 The eight black strips are the screen \, one per 8-pixel row. They are cnv objects with the text as their label \, hence pd oled-decode's join., f 58;
#X text 640 800 Laid out like the front panel: aux \, knobs 1-4 \, screen \, encoder \, volume \, keys. Below this line is plumbing \, invisible on main-dev.pd., f 58;
#X text 1240 680 The bench row is the display bench. open-screen-log reads back a boot that finishes before you can look., f 58;
#X obj 40 530 bng 24 250 50 0 empty clock beat 0 -14 0 11 -262144 -1 -1;
#X floatatom 140 530 5 0 0 1 tempo-bus tempo -;
#X floatatom 280 530 3 0 0 1 aux-LED led -;
#X symbolatom 420 530 11 0 0 0 - \$0-ledcol -;
#X obj 580 530 bng 24 250 50 0 \$0-auxtap empty aux-tap 0 -14 0 11 -262144 -1 -1;
#X obj 660 530 bng 24 250 50 0 \$0-b-start empty start 0 -14 0 11 -262144 -1 -1;
#X obj 740 530 bng 24 250 50 0 \$0-b-stop empty stop 0 -14 0 11 -262144 -1 -1;
#X obj 820 530 bng 24 250 50 0 \$0-b-panic empty panic 0 -14 0 11 -262144 -1 -1;
#X obj 920 530 bng 24 250 50 0 \$0-b-thi empty bpm-hi 0 -14 0 11 -262144 -1 -1;
#X obj 1000 530 bng 24 250 50 0 \$0-b-tlo empty bpm-lo 0 -14 0 11 -262144 -1 -1;
#N canvas 40 40 1400 1120 bench5 0;
#X text 20 20 The tempo bench row. The tempo control is knob 1 itself \, so this holds what a knob cannot do., f 58;
#X obj 20 150 r \$0-auxtap;
#X obj 20 190 t b b;
#X msg 20 240 1;
#X obj 20 320 s aux;
#X obj 180 190 del 120;
#X msg 180 240 0;
#X obj 460 150 r \$0-b-start;
#X obj 460 190 s start;
#X obj 620 150 r \$0-b-stop;
#X obj 620 190 s stop;
#X obj 780 150 r \$0-b-panic;
#X obj 780 190 s panic;
#X obj 960 150 r \$0-b-thi;
#X msg 960 190 5000;
#X obj 960 240 s tempo;
#X obj 1120 150 r \$0-b-tlo;
#X msg 1120 190 0;
#X obj 1120 240 s tempo;
#X text 20 400 The aux tap is a press and a release 120 ms apart \, as mother sends them: aux is the keyboard's modifier and uses both edges. The panel's toggle takes two clicks to make one press., f 58;
#X text 20 530 bpm-hi and bpm-lo are 5000 and 0 against a legal 5 to 600: each must clamp and raise its own alert \, and pressing one twice must be silent the second time., f 58;
#X text 20 660 start \, stop and panic: on a Mac with no rig \, nothing else sends them., f 58;
#X obj 20 760 r led;
#X obj 20 800 select 0 1 2 3 4 5 6 7;
#X msg 20 850 symbol off;
#X msg 140 850 symbol red;
#X msg 260 850 symbol yellow;
#X msg 400 850 symbol green;
#X msg 540 850 symbol cyan;
#X msg 680 850 symbol dark-blue;
#X msg 820 850 symbol pink;
#X msg 960 850 symbol white;
#X obj 20 950 s \$0-ledcol;
#X text 20 1160 Two BPM readouts \, meant to disagree: tempo-bus shows what was requested (5000) and the OLED what u_tempo did with it (600). u_tempo never re-emits the clamped value \, which would loop., f 58;
#X text 20 1010 The panel names the LED color as g_led meant it \, beside the number mother receives on led., f 58;
